 # Changelog
 
 All notable changes to Fluent HTML will be documented in this file.
+
+## [9.0.0] - One migration: selectors mean what htmx reads, a gated prune, one nonce spelling, typed form values
+
+Breaking, in one codemod-first migration with no aliases and no shims. A removed name fails as a plain TS2339/TS2305, a bare selector word names its fix, and each codemod reports what it will not rewrite as SKIP. Run, in order:
+
+1. Pre-7 repos only: `npm run codemod:canonical -- <tsconfig>`.
+2. Install fluent-html 9.0.0.
+3. `npm run codemod:prune-9 -- <tsconfig>`: the removed names, the moved imports and `ForEachElse`.
+4. `npm run codemod:nonce-bag -- <tsconfig>`: the nonce options bag.
+5. `scripts/codemod/bare-selector.ts`: bare selector words.
+6. `npm run codemod:form-values-9 -- <tsconfig>`: it keys on the 9.0.0 diagnostics, so it runs after the install.
+7. `npm run guidelines:pull`: every vendored `fluent-html.md` still teaches `Repeat(3, () => Br())`.
+
+`codemod:prune-9` and `codemod:nonce-bag` both rewrite fluent-html import declarations, so run them one after the other; the npm codemods take `--dry`. Each section below gives its codemod's measured dry run. Per-item rationale and evidence: [`project/research/v8.2.0/`](project/research/v8.2.0/).
+
+### 💥 Changed: a bare selector word means what htmx reads it as, in every sink (RFC-B-04)
+
+A bare word meant `#id` in `Partial` and a tag selector in `hx()` options: `hx(…, { target: "team-list" })` swapped out its own button and left two `[id=team-list]` on both bundles.
+
+- `HxTarget` loses its `string` arm. A `target`, `include`, `indicator` or `disable` is an `Id`, an htmx keyword (`this`, `body`, `host`, `next`, `previous`, …), an HTML tag name, a `closest`/`find`/`findAll`/`next`/`previous`/`global` form, or a punctuated CSS selector.
+- `select` and `hxResponse().reselect()` take the new `HxSelect` (tag names and punctuated CSS only): htmx applies them to the response with `querySelectorAll`, so `"this"` emptied the target with no console line (10/10 keyword rows).
+- A bare id-like word (`"team-list"`) or a value typed `string` no longer compiles, and the error names the fix on line 1 (8 of 10 wrong guesses): `use ids.x for an element id; a bare word is an HTML tag or htmx keyword; type a string variable as HxTarget`. In a select sink: `hx-select reads plain CSS on the response: use ids.x for an element id; htmx keywords (this, next, closest ...) select nothing here`.
+- `HxSelect` is exported from `fluent-html` and `fluent-html/htmx`, and the selector helpers (`id`, `clss`, `closest`, `find`, `next`, `previous`) return their literal forms.
+- **Codemod:** `scripts/codemod/bare-selector.ts` rewrites `Partial("<word>")` (below) and reports every other site. Measured on 15 live repos: 0 rewrites and 2 reported sites, everyframe-composer `studio.voice.view.ts:326` (a computed `.join(", ")`) and gzs/stem-50 `src/shared/ui/search.ts:6` (`include?: string` in a `ListRoute` type, 4 errors where route callables are assigned to it); each is a 2-line fix that types the value as `HxTarget`.
+
+### 💥 Changed: `f.radio`, `f.hidden` and `f.checkbox` values are checked against the bound field (RFC-E-04)
+
+8.2.0's `f.select` check now covers the other value-taking bindings. A valued checkbox on a boolean field stays open (`f.checkbox("terms", "yes")`, the 8.1.1 group shape).
+
+- A generic helper whose binding is `FormBinding<T>` with `T extends …` cannot prove its value and now fails TS2345: `npm run codemod:form-values-9 -- <tsconfig>` wraps that argument in `String(…)` (the 8.x unchecked behavior) and reports any other shape. Typing the helper's binding as the concrete request type keeps the check instead.
+- Dry run: home-page `content-panel.components.ts:60` 1/1 rewritten, 0 errors left; the 15 other canonical repos and the template have 0 hits.
+
+### 💥 Removed: two dead second spellings and four duplicate root exports (RFC-C-02)
+
+| Removed | Use instead |
+|---|---|
+| `Form().multipart()` | `.setEnctype("multipart/form-data")` (byte-identical) |
+| `Repeat(n, f)` (root and `fluent-html/control`) | `ForEach(n, f)` (byte-identical; `Repeat` already delegated to it) |
+| `extractId`, `extractSelector` from `"fluent-html"` | `"fluent-html/ids"` |
+| `EVENT_TABLE`, `HTMX_EVENTS` from `"fluent-html"` | `"fluent-html/behaviors"` |
 
+- Each removed name fails as a plain TS2339/TS2305 with no suggestion.
+- `codemod:prune-9` rewrites them and reports namespace members, re-exports, value references to `Repeat` and `Repeat` with a parameterized function as SKIP.
+- Dry runs, compiled: the template (0 edits / 339 files) and the 15 canonical-era repos 0 edits for these names, tsc identical; storysell-system, storysell-system-define-feature-exp, gzs/inovacije and jt-vault 6 edits, none adding a compile error (jt-vault through the new `typesVersions`).
+
+### 💥 Removed: `Partial`'s bare-word `#` rewrite (RFC-B-04)
+
+`Partial("main", …)` now targets the `<main>` element (8.x emitted `#main`, which missed a page `<main>` with no id). `Partial` is one signature, so a bad target prints its hint on line 1 instead of under "No overload matches this call"; return types are unchanged (`Tag & Rooted<N>` for an `Id`). The codemod rewrites `Partial("<word>")` to `Partial("#<word>")`, which keeps the 8.x bytes (lib 8/8 fixtures; 0 sites in the template and 15 live repos), and reports keyword targets such as `Partial("body")` instead of guessing.
+
+### 💥 Removed: `ForEachElse` (RFC-E-07)
+
+`IfNotEmptyElse(xs, (rows) => ForEach(rows, f), e)` is the one empty-state form, and eslint-plugin-fluent-html 4.3.0's `prefer-if-not-empty` already autofixes `ForEachElse` to it. `codemod:prune-9` rewrites any call left (a View fallback becomes `() => e`): everyframe-composer 1/1 compiles and renders byte-identical in the non-empty and the empty state; time-to-live's 1 site is reported (no install). The import fails as a plain TS2305 with no suggestion, and 0 of 12 measured agent runs reached for `ForEachElse` first.
+
+### 💥 Removed: the CSP-nonce options bag (RFC-C-03)
+
+The nonce has one spelling: the `*WithNonce` form is the plain form with the nonce first. `render(view, { nonce })`, the `nonce` key on `renderToStream`/`renderToIterable` options and the `RenderOptions` type are removed; `RenderStreamOptions` keeps `chunkSize` and `highWaterMark`. Census: 89 `renderWithNonce`/`renderToStreamWithNonce` sites in 16/16 canonical repos, 0 bag sites outside the library's own tests.
+
+- **Migration.** `npm run codemod:nonce-bag -- <tsconfig>` rewrites `render(v, { nonce })` to `renderWithNonce(nonce, v)` and `renderToStream(v, { nonce, chunkSize })` to `renderToStreamWithNonce(nonce, v, { chunkSize })`. It reports `renderToIterable` nonces and bags it cannot see into (passed by reference, spread) as SKIP. Those shapes still type-check after the removal and drop the nonce at runtime, where the browser then blocks the script, so treat every SKIP as a must-fix.
+- 7 of 10 measured bag shapes fail tsc (`'nonce' does not exist in type …`). Dry runs: the template, competify, everyframe and fluent-html-home-page 0 rewrites, 0 skips.
+- One untyped-JS change: `render(v, {})` gains a trailing `"\n"` (0 such callers in the org).
+
+### ✨ Added: `renderToStreamWithNonce` is variadic and takes chunking options (RFC-C-03)
+
+`renderToStreamWithNonce(nonce, ...views)` mirrors `renderWithNonce`; it took one view, and `(nonce, a, b)` was TS2554. `renderToStreamWithNonce(nonce, view, { chunkSize, highWaterMark })` is the render-time path for a nonce plus tuned chunking, chunk-for-chunk equal to 8.1.0's `renderToStream(view, { nonce, chunkSize, highWaterMark })` (6/6). Without it, 3/3 agents fell back to per-element `.setNonce()` on the shared tree.
+
+### ✨ Added: subpath types resolve under `moduleResolution: node10` (RFC-C-02)
+
+`package.json` gains `typesVersions` for `core`, `ids`, `behaviors` and `control`. A `module: commonjs` consumer importing `extractSelector` from `"fluent-html/ids"` got TS2307; it now compiles, and NodeNext resolution is unchanged. 4 of 58 fleet repos resolve as node10, and `codemod:prune-9` moves their root imports to these subpaths.
+
+### 🧊 Kept: what agents write first (RFC-C-02)
+
+The census-zero setters and utilities stay: 149/222 recorded guesses compile on 8.1.0 and on 9.0.0, against 12/222 after a census-only prune. `containerQuery()`, the root `setDevChecks` and `setMicrodata()` stay too: the first two are first guesses in 1/13 and 3/21 leak-free runs, and `setMicrodata`'s closed key bag catches the typos `addAttribute` would not. This replaces 8.0.0's "candidates for deletion in a future major if the census stays at zero": a name now leaves only when its removal draws no suggestion, at least 20 leak-free runs per condition never write it, and `test/prune-gate.test.ts` stays green.
+
 ## [8.2.0] - Additions: opt-in class merge, getId, IfNotEmpty, .size(), typed select values, htmx 4 swap modifiers
 
 Additive. Every valid 8.1.1 call compiles and renders the same bytes, and the class merge stays off until an app turns it on. Two new checks reject code that was already wrong: a literal `f.select` option value the bound field cannot take is a compile error (0 new tsc errors in 15 canonical repos and the template), and under dev checks a required select whose own markup preselects a value nobody chose throws at render. eslint-plugin-fluent-html 4.3.0, published after this release, adds `prefer-if-not-empty` and `prefer-size`, which move existing code onto `IfNotEmpty` and `.size()`. Per-item rationale and evidence: [`project/research/v8.2.0/`](project/research/v8.2.0/).
